    {
      "title": "[P1] Recheck workspace ownership before widening grants",
      "body": "If a workspace is transferred after migration, the former owner still owns the historical report and can call this endpoint; the code then mutates the current workspace's grants without checking `Workspace.owner_id`. This allows a user who no longer controls the workspace to grant workspace-wide access, bypassing the required authorization path in `AGENTS.md:68-70`.",
      "confidence_score": 0.97,
      "priority": 1,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/backend/app/services/migration/reports.py",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 142,
          "end": 147
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P1] Submit the field choices shown by default",
      "body": "When the reviewer leaves the displayed defaults unchanged, every select renders `\"a\"` via its fallback but `fields` remains empty, so this sends `{}`. The backend then marks the conflict resolved without applying any values; because the canonical member can be member B, the stored result can contradict the visible A selections and cannot subsequently be corrected through this conflict.",
      "confidence_score": 0.99,
      "priority": 1,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/frontend/src/components/view/migration-review-view/MigrationConflictCard.tsx",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 85,
          "end": 88
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Remove a successfully widened grant from the actions",
      "body": "After a successful widening, reloading cannot remove the action because `grant_changes` is immutable report history and `GrantChangeRow` renders every entry unconditionally. The same Widen button therefore remains available, and clicking it again reaches the now-deleted section grant and shows a generic 404 error; track completed pairs locally or return current actionability from the API instead of relying on this reload.",
      "confidence_score": 0.98,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/frontend/src/hooks/useMigrationReviewStore.ts",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 61,
          "end": 64
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Translate grant roles and restrictions",
      "body": "The API's raw values such as `editor`, `viewer`, `gallery`, and `sources` are rendered directly, so this new dialog remains partly English/internal-key text in the German locale. Route these values through the existing role/domain translation keys as required by `AGENTS.md:125-129`.",
      "confidence_score": 0.99,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/frontend/src/components/view/migration-review-view/GrantWidenDialog.tsx",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 36,
          "end": 43
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P3] Gate the checklist badge on pending conflicts",
      "body": "When there is an unacknowledged report but no pending conflict, `pendingCount` is positive while `pendingConflicts.length` is zero, causing the Checklist tab to display a destructive `0` badge. Use the conflict count for both the condition and displayed value so the badge represents that tab's contents.",
      "confidence_score": 0.99,
      "priority": 3,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/frontend/src/components/view/migration-review-view/MigrationReviewView.tsx",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 238,
          "end": 240
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "overall_correctness": "patch is incorrect",
  "overall_explanation": "The new grant-widening endpoint permits stale report owners to change access after ownership transfer, and the conflict UI can irreversibly resolve conflicts without applying its displayed choices. Additional action-state, localization, and badge defects also affect the new review workflow.",
  "overall_confidence_score": 0.98
}
